+// for the host GPU. A guest thread posts physical ranges into one of kMaxSlots
+// slots; the bytes the host GPU copy holds newer than guest memory there
+// (SharedMemory::ForEachGpuNewerPart) are copied by the GPU in the background
+// and kept here, on the host. Nothing is written to guest memory: title code
+// takes the bytes (AwaitGuestSnapshot) and writes them itself when it chooses.
+//
+// Threads: guest threads post, await, flush and drop under
+// GuestSnapshots::mutex (posting also takes the global critical region inside
+// it). The command processor thread never waits for that mutex while running:
+// it takes posts lock-free (an exchange of posted[]) and delivers with
+// try_lock; it locks the mutex only to start and stop the service.
